{"wiki_catalogs":[{"id":"38158162-a0a3-4091-ba41-644b59a8d8d1","repo_id":"6bc5aca4-dd86-4008-9d0b-e2fbaaaf7385","name":"Getting Started","description":"getting-started","prompt":"Create comprehensive getting started content for this web development learning cohort. Explain the project's educational purpose, learning objectives, and how to navigate through the weekly progression. Document prerequisites including basic computer literacy and text editor setup. Provide step-by-step instructions for running the examples locally in a browser. Include an overview of the curriculum structure from HTML/CSS fundamentals to JavaScript and Node.js concepts. Make it accessible for beginners while establishing the foundation for progressive learning.","progress_status":"completed","dependent_files":"Warmup-Video/Zerodha.html","gmt_create":"2026-09-30T22:47:45.710408+05:30","gmt_modified":"2026-09-30T22:48:25.207851+05:30","raw_data":"WikiEncrypted:"},{"id":"8c0561a0-6c97-4a19-89a4-5b56fd7c26e5","repo_id":"6bc5aca4-dd86-4008-9d0b-e2fbaaaf7385","name":"Week 1: HTML \u0026 CSS Fundamentals","description":"week-1-html-css","prompt":"Create comprehensive documentation for Week 1 covering HTML and CSS fundamentals. Explain the responsive navigation bar implementation using Flexbox layout system. Document the VS Code website recreation project including semantic HTML structure, modern CSS practices, Google Fonts integration with Montserrat typography, and interactive hover effects. Detail the flexbox properties used for alignment and spacing. Include practical examples of the navigation component, button styling, and responsive design principles. Address common CSS challenges and best practices for beginners.","order":1,"progress_status":"completed","dependent_files":"Week-1/VS-Code/Index.html,Week-1/VS-Code/style.css","gmt_create":"2026-09-30T22:47:45.710896+05:30","gmt_modified":"2026-09-30T22:48:15.909517+05:30","raw_data":"WikiEncrypted:"},{"id":"4576358e-c3e7-4e26-8570-119814ea9a19","repo_id":"6bc5aca4-dd86-4008-9d0b-e2fbaaaf7385","name":"Week 2: JavaScript Basics","description":"week-2-javascript-basics","prompt":"Develop detailed documentation for Week 2 JavaScript fundamentals. Cover function declarations and parameter handling from index.js, conditional statements and decision making from condition.js, and object property manipulation from Object-Key.js. Explain JavaScript programming concepts including functions, if-else statements, nested objects, array operations (filter and map methods), and data processing patterns. Include concrete code examples demonstrating function parameters, age verification logic, and student object manipulation. Address JavaScript scope, parameter passing, and object-oriented basics for beginners.","order":2,"progress_status":"completed","dependent_files":"Week-2/Javascript-Basic/index.js,Week-2/Javascript-Basic/condition.js,Week-2/Javascript-Basic/Object-Key.js","gmt_create":"2026-09-30T22:47:45.711263+05:30","gmt_modified":"2026-09-30T22:48:14.343694+05:30","raw_data":"WikiEncrypted:"},{"id":"6c7fcf08-c09d-4193-abb5-283dcd0de9c8","repo_id":"6bc5aca4-dd86-4008-9d0b-e2fbaaaf7385","name":"Week 3: Node.js Introduction","description":"week-3-nodejs-introduction","prompt":"Create comprehensive documentation for Week 3 introducing Node.js server-side JavaScript. Explain file system operations using the fs module, synchronous file reading with UTF-8 encoding, and console output for debugging. Document the Node.js environment setup, file path resolution, and error handling for file operations. Include practical examples of reading text files, handling file content, and understanding the difference between client-side and server-side JavaScript. Address Node.js runtime requirements and basic file I/O patterns for beginners transitioning from browser-based JavaScript.","order":3,"progress_status":"completed","dependent_files":"Week-3/Work/Index.js,Week-3/Work/A.txt","gmt_create":"2026-09-30T22:47:45.711584+05:30","gmt_modified":"2026-09-30T22:48:34.456322+05:30","raw_data":"WikiEncrypted:"},{"id":"149b463a-a832-4fb1-84b5-d3b1e4712148","repo_id":"6bc5aca4-dd86-4008-9d0b-e2fbaaaf7385","name":"Week 3.1: DOM Manipulation","description":"week-3-dom-manipulation","prompt":"Develop detailed documentation for DOM manipulation techniques. Explain dynamic content generation using JavaScript arrays, filtering and mapping operations on data structures, and real-time DOM updates without page reloads. Document the relationship between HTML structure and JavaScript manipulation, event handling patterns, and dynamic element creation. Include practical examples of array filtering for student data, dynamic HTML generation, and interactive UI updates. Address DOM performance considerations, best practices for efficient manipulation, and common pitfalls for beginners working with dynamic content.","order":4,"progress_status":"completed","dependent_files":"Week-3.1/index.html,Week-3.1/script.js","gmt_create":"2026-09-30T22:47:45.711862+05:30","gmt_modified":"2026-09-30T22:48:41.305909+05:30","raw_data":"WikiEncrypted:"}],"wiki_items":[{"catalog_id":"4576358e-c3e7-4e26-8570-119814ea9a19","title":"Week 2: JavaScript Basics","description":"week-2-javascript-basics","extend":"{}","progress_status":"completed","repo_id":"6bc5aca4-dd86-4008-9d0b-e2fbaaaf7385","reference_count":0,"id":"49d8b8c8-aa8f-4350-a89e-47d1b55b2381","gmt_create":"2026-09-30T22:48:14.339852+05:30","gmt_modified":"2026-09-30T22:48:14.343863+05:30"},{"catalog_id":"8c0561a0-6c97-4a19-89a4-5b56fd7c26e5","title":"Week 1: HTML \u0026 CSS Fundamentals","description":"week-1-html-css","extend":"{}","progress_status":"completed","repo_id":"6bc5aca4-dd86-4008-9d0b-e2fbaaaf7385","reference_count":0,"id":"1c12267b-c4c8-424b-ae8c-ac5aab6168f1","gmt_create":"2026-09-30T22:48:15.905582+05:30","gmt_modified":"2026-09-30T22:48:15.909682+05:30"},{"catalog_id":"38158162-a0a3-4091-ba41-644b59a8d8d1","title":"Getting Started","description":"getting-started","extend":"{}","progress_status":"completed","repo_id":"6bc5aca4-dd86-4008-9d0b-e2fbaaaf7385","reference_count":0,"id":"d870ed34-5361-4dd2-b86f-d8f20e8e71f0","gmt_create":"2026-09-30T22:48:25.2051+05:30","gmt_modified":"2026-09-30T22:48:25.207942+05:30"},{"catalog_id":"6c7fcf08-c09d-4193-abb5-283dcd0de9c8","title":"Week 3: Node.js Introduction","description":"week-3-nodejs-introduction","extend":"{}","progress_status":"completed","repo_id":"6bc5aca4-dd86-4008-9d0b-e2fbaaaf7385","reference_count":0,"id":"082567a1-0199-4a0b-b108-0592af5297ac","gmt_create":"2026-09-30T22:48:34.454663+05:30","gmt_modified":"2026-09-30T22:48:34.45641+05:30"},{"catalog_id":"149b463a-a832-4fb1-84b5-d3b1e4712148","title":"Week 3.1: DOM Manipulation","description":"week-3-dom-manipulation","extend":"{}","progress_status":"completed","repo_id":"6bc5aca4-dd86-4008-9d0b-e2fbaaaf7385","reference_count":0,"id":"e16cd95a-6dc1-4e28-bf5e-c97dc71488bb","gmt_create":"2026-09-30T22:48:41.301688+05:30","gmt_modified":"2026-09-30T22:48:41.30609+05:30"}],"wiki_overview":{"content":"\u003cblog\u003e\n\n# Comprehensive Project Analysis: Web Development Learning Cohort\n\n## 1. Project Introduction\n\n### Purpose Statement\nThis project serves as a comprehensive learning portfolio for web development fundamentals, structured as a progressive curriculum spanning multiple weeks. It demonstrates the evolution from basic HTML/CSS to JavaScript programming concepts and file system operations.\n\n### Core Goals and Objectives\n- **Educational Progression**: Guide learners through fundamental web development concepts week by week\n- **Practical Implementation**: Provide hands-on examples of HTML structure, CSS styling, and JavaScript functionality\n- **Real-world Application**: Demonstrate practical UI components like navigation bars and interactive elements\n- **Skill Building**: Progress from static pages to dynamic content manipulation\n\n### Target Audience\n- Beginner web developers\n- Students learning front-end development\n- Individuals transitioning into full-stack development\n- Anyone seeking foundational web development skills\n\n## 2. Technical Architecture\n\nThe project follows a **progressive learning architecture** where each week builds upon previous concepts:\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    A[Week 1: HTML/CSS Basics] --\u003e B[Week 2: JavaScript Fundamentals]\n    B --\u003e C[Week 3: Node.js \u0026 File System]\n    C --\u003e D[Week 3.1: DOM Manipulation]\n    \n    E[Warmup: Zerodha Clone] --\u003e A\n    \n    subgraph \"Frontend Components\"\n        F[HTML Structure] --\u003e G[CSS Styling]\n        G --\u003e H[JavaScript Logic]\n    end\n    \n    subgraph \"Learning Progression\"\n        I[Static Pages] --\u003e J[Interactive Elements]\n        J --\u003e K[Dynamic Content]\n    end\n```\n\n### Component Breakdown\n- **Static Frontend Layer**: HTML documents with embedded CSS\n- **Client-side Scripting**: Vanilla JavaScript for interactivity\n- **Server-side Operations**: Node.js file system operations\n- **Progressive Enhancement**: Each week adds new capabilities\n\n### Design Patterns\n- **Modular Organization**: Separate files for HTML, CSS, and JavaScript\n- **Component-based Structure**: Reusable UI patterns (navigation bars, buttons)\n- **Functional Programming**: Function-based JavaScript logic\n- **File-based Architecture**: Organized by weekly learning modules\n\n## 3. Key Implementation\n\n### Main Entry Points\n- **Warmup Landing Page**: `Warmup-Video/Zerodha.html` - Demonstrates responsive layout and modern UI design\n- **VS Code Documentation Site**: `Week-1/VS-Code/Index.html` - Complex navigation and styling implementation\n- **JavaScript Fundamentals**: `Week-2/Javascript-Basic/index.js` - Core programming concepts\n- **DOM Manipulation**: `Week-3.1/script.js` - Dynamic content generation and manipulation\n\n### Core Modules\n\n#### HTML Structure Module\n```mermaid\nclassDiagram\n    class HTMLStructure {\n        +Header Navigation\n        +Main Content Area\n        +Footer Elements\n        +Responsive Layout\n    }\n    \n    class CSSStyling {\n        +Flexbox Layouts\n        +Custom Properties\n        +Hover Effects\n        +Typography\n    }\n    \n    class JavaScriptLogic {\n        +Event Handling\n        +Data Processing\n        +DOM Manipulation\n        +File Operations\n    }\n    \n    HTMLStructure --\u003e CSSStyling\n    HTMLStructure --\u003e JavaScriptLogic\n```\n\n#### JavaScript Functionality Module\n- **Basic Functions**: Function declarations and parameter handling\n- **Conditional Logic**: If-else statements and decision making\n- **Object Manipulation**: Property access and nested object handling\n- **Array Operations**: Filter, map, and data transformation methods\n\n### Configuration Approach\n- **No Build Tools**: Pure vanilla development without frameworks or bundlers\n- **Direct File References**: Simple script and stylesheet linking\n- **External Dependencies**: Google Fonts integration for typography\n- **Browser Compatibility**: Standard HTML5 and ES6 features\n\n### External Dependencies\n- **Google Fonts API**: Montserrat font family integration\n- **Node.js File System**: Built-in fs module for file operations\n- **Browser APIs**: DOM manipulation and event handling\n\n### Integration Points\n- **CSS Framework Integration**: Custom stylesheets with external font resources\n- **JavaScript Runtime**: Browser console for debugging and output\n- **File System Access**: Node.js environment for server-side operations\n\n## 4. Key Features\n\n### Functionality Overview\n\n#### Responsive Navigation System\n- **Flexible Layout**: Flexbox-based navigation bar with logo and menu items\n- **Interactive Elements**: Hover effects and cursor feedback\n- **Search Integration**: Search input field with download functionality\n\n#### Interactive User Interface\n- **Dynamic Content Generation**: JavaScript-driven list creation\n- **Data Filtering**: Array filtering based on specific criteria\n- **DOM Manipulation**: Real-time content updates without page reload\n\n#### Educational Progression System\n```mermaid\nstateDiagram-v2\n    [*] --\u003e StaticHTML\n    StaticHTML --\u003e CSSStyling: Learn Selectors\n    CSSStyling --\u003e JavaScriptBasics: Add Interactivity\n    JavaScriptBasics --\u003e AdvancedJS: Master Concepts\n    AdvancedJS --\u003e NodeJS: Server-side Programming\n    NodeJS --\u003e CompleteProject: Final Application\n```\n\n### Implementation Highlights\n\n#### Modern UI Components (`Week-1/VS-Code/style.css`)\n- **Flexbox Layouts**: Responsive navigation and content alignment\n- **Custom Typography**: Google Fonts integration with optical sizing\n- **Interactive States**: Hover effects and transition animations\n- **Color Systems**: Consistent color palette with semantic naming\n\n#### JavaScript Programming Concepts (`Week-2/Javascript-Basic/`)\n- **Function Declarations**: Parameter passing and return values\n- **Conditional Statements**: Age verification and eligibility checking\n- **Object Properties**: Nested object access and manipulation\n- **Array Methods**: Filter and map operations for data processing\n\n#### File System Operations (`Week-3/Work/Index.js`)\n- **Synchronous File Reading**: Using Node.js fs module\n- **UTF-8 Encoding**: Proper text file handling\n- **Console Output**: Debugging and content verification\n\n### Feature Architecture Diagrams\n\n#### Data Flow Architecture\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant User\n    participant HTML as HTML Document\n    participant JS as JavaScript Engine\n    participant DOM as DOM Tree\n    \n    User-\u003e\u003e+HTML: Load Page\n    HTML-\u003e\u003e+JS: Execute Script\n    JS-\u003e\u003e+DOM: Query Elements\n    DOM--\u003e\u003e-JS: Return Elements\n    JS-\u003e\u003e+DOM: Update Content\n    DOM--\u003e\u003e-User: Render Changes\n```\n\n#### Component Relationship Map\n```mermaid\ngraph LR\n    A[Zerodha Landing Page] --\u003e B[Navigation Bar]\n    A --\u003e C[Hero Section]\n    A --\u003e D[Call-to-Action]\n    \n    E[VS Code Site] --\u003e F[Complex Navbar]\n    E --\u003e G[Content Sections]\n    E --\u003e H[Interactive Elements]\n    \n    I[JavaScript Basics] --\u003e J[Functions]\n    I --\u003e K[Conditionals]\n    I --\u003e L[Objects]\n    \n    M[DOM Manipulation] --\u003e N[Array Operations]\n    M --\u003e O[Element Creation]\n```\n\n## 5. Conclusion and Recommendations\n\n### Project Architecture Summary\nThis learning cohort demonstrates a well-structured progression from basic web development concepts to more advanced topics. The modular organization allows learners to build confidence incrementally while developing practical skills in HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.\n\n### Key Characteristics\n- **Educational Focus**: Clear progression from simple to complex concepts\n- **Practical Examples**: Real-world UI components and interactions\n- **Clean Separation**: Distinct files for structure, style, and behavior\n- **Modern Practices**: Use of contemporary web standards and techniques\n\n### Architectural Strengths\n- **Incremental Complexity**: Each week introduces manageable new concepts\n- **Real-world Applications**: Practical examples that mirror industry standards\n- **Clear Organization**: Logical file structure that supports learning progression\n- **Hands-on Learning**: Direct code examples with immediate results\n\n### Potential Improvement Areas\n- **Add Version Control**: Implement Git for tracking progress and changes\n- **Include Testing**: Add unit tests for JavaScript functions\n- **Enhance Accessibility**: Improve ARIA labels and keyboard navigation\n- **Mobile Responsiveness**: Add media queries for better mobile support\n\n### Actionable Recommendations\n1. **Implement a Build Process**: Consider adding a simple bundler like Vite or Parcel\n2. **Add CSS Framework**: Integrate Tailwind CSS or Bootstrap for consistent styling\n3. **Create Reusable Components**: Extract common UI patterns into reusable modules\n4. **Document API Usage**: Add JSDoc comments for JavaScript functions\n5. **Performance Optimization**: Implement lazy loading and code splitting\n\n### Next Steps for Project Evolution\n- **Week 4+ Planning**: Plan introduction to React/Vue for component-based architecture\n- **Backend Integration**: Add Express.js for server-side functionality\n- **Database Connection**: Implement MongoDB or PostgreSQL for data persistence\n- **Deployment Strategy**: Set up CI/CD pipeline for automated deployment\n- **Advanced Topics**: Cover authentication, authorization, and security best practices\n\n---\n\n**Sources:**\n- [Zerodha.html](Warmup-Video/Zerodha.html)\n- [Index.html](Week-1/VS-Code/Index.html)\n- [style.css](Week-1/VS-Code/style.css)\n- [index.js](Week-2/Javascript-Basic/index.js)\n- [condition.js](Week-2/Javascript-Basic/condition.js)\n- [Object-Key.js](Week-2/Javascript-Basic/Object-Key.js)\n- [Index.js](Week-3/Work/Index.js)\n- [script.js](Week-3.1/script.js)\n\n\u003c/blog\u003e","gmt_create":"2026-09-30T22:47:08.690265+05:30","gmt_modified":"2026-09-30T22:47:08.690265+05:30","id":"f955de95-412c-44bd-9680-c0ab435a7b1a","repo_id":"6bc5aca4-dd86-4008-9d0b-e2fbaaaf7385"},"wiki_readme":{"content":"No readme file","gmt_create":"2026-09-30T22:46:40.723935+05:30","gmt_modified":"2026-09-30T22:46:40.723935+05:30","id":"8aefe88b-a5d4-4096-a446-a62442c355c4","repo_id":"6bc5aca4-dd86-4008-9d0b-e2fbaaaf7385"},"wiki_repo":{"id":"6bc5aca4-dd86-4008-9d0b-e2fbaaaf7385","name":"Cohort-1","progress_status":"completed","wiki_present_status":"COMPLETED","optimized_catalog":"\".\\n├── Notes/\\n├── Warmup-Video/\\n│   └── Zerodha.html\\n├── Week-1/\\n│   ├── Notes/\\n│   └── VS-Code/\\n│       ├── Index.html\\n│       └── style.css\\n├── Week-2/Javascript-Basic/\\n│   ├── Object-Key.js\\n│   ├── condition.js\\n│   └── index.js\\n├── Week-3/\\n│   ├── Notes/\\n│   └── Work/\\n│       ├── A.txt\\n│       └── Index.js\\n└── Week-3.1/\\n    ├── index.html\\n    └── script.js\\n\"","current_document_structure":"WikiEncrypted:","catalogue_think_content":"WikiEncrypted:","recovery_checkpoint":"wiki_generation_completed","last_commit_id":"9706023cd96000d8de2534fdcacb888c4ea52204","last_commit_update":"2026-09-30T22:48:41.312369+05:30","gmt_create":"2026-09-30T22:46:40.330979+05:30","gmt_modified":"2026-09-30T22:48:41.312369+05:30","extend_info":"{\"language\":\"en\",\"active\":true,\"branch\":\"main\",\"shareStatus\":\"\",\"server_error_code\":\"\",\"cosy_version\":\"\"}"}}